</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>One button, and it is Copy</h2>
		<p>Nobody reads a snippet page. They scan for the one that matches, copy it, and leave — so the card is built around that: the title says what it is <em>for</em> (not what it is called), one line says when to use it, the code is clipped to seven lines with a fade, and Copy is the only button.</p>
		<p>It is the system's own <a href="/components/code/">copy behaviour</a> — <code>data-im-copy</code>, which writes to the clipboard and changes the label to "Copied" for a moment. No script of this page's own.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>im-snippet</code></td><td>The card. Fills on hover, like everything else.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-snippet-lang</code></td><td>The language, with a dot in <code>--im-repo-lang</code> — the same dot the <a href="/collections/project/card/">project card</a> uses, so one colour means one language everywhere on the site.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-snippet-body</code></td><td>Clipped to <code>--im-snippet-lines</code> (7) with a fade at the bottom. A card is a preview; the whole thing is one click away.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-snippet-foot</code></td><td>The kind chip on the left, Copy pushed to the right.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>

		<h2>Why not a gist</h2>
		<p>Because a gist is somebody else's page, it does not match the site, it does not work offline, it cannot be searched from here, and it disappears when the host decides. A snippet that matters enough to keep matters enough to host.</p>

		<h2>Details that matter</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Title it by the problem</strong> — "fluid type without a media query", not "clamp()". The reader is searching for the problem.</li>
			<li><strong>Keep them short.</strong> If it does not fit in seven lines it is a <a href="/collections/post/">post</a> with a snippet in it.</li>
			<li><strong>Test everything on the page.</strong> A snippet collection with one broken entry is a snippet collection nobody trusts.</li>
			<li><strong>The copy button copies the source</strong>, not the highlighted HTML — <code>data-im-copy</code> takes the raw text.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
